course: dictionary
lesson: 9501
title: The steppe
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A steppe is a huge, flat area of grassland with very few trees. You find steppes mostly in eastern Europe and Asia. Steppe is a noun, so you can write a steppe or steppes.
explain: Read the clues around the word. «There were few trees on the cold steppe» tells you the steppe has few trees, so it must be open, grassy land. Check it by swapping in your meaning: «There were few trees on the cold grassland» still makes sense, so you have it right.
explain: Other places work the same way. The prairie in North America and the pampas in South America are also huge grasslands. Geographers call these grassland biomes, and the steppe is one of them.
fact: A steppe is a huge, flat area of grassland with few trees.
fact: The steppe has hot summers, cold winters and little rain.
fact: In history, nomads rode horses across the steppes.
fact: «Ukraine's black earth» was built over thousands of years by steppe grass roots dying and rotting into the ground.
fact: The prairie in North America and the pampas in South America are grassland biomes like the steppe.
exercise: «Once the steppe covered much of southern Ukraine.» What is a steppe? | A deep forest full of tall trees | *A huge, flat area of grassland with few trees | A high mountain range covered in snow | A large lake with sandy shores
exercise: «There were few trees on the cold steppe, so giant bones were the best building material they had.» Why did people use giant bones to build? | Because bones are lighter than wood | *Because there were few trees to build with | Because bones grow on trees | Because they wanted the steppe to look pretty
exercise: Which kind of place is the steppe? | A busy city by the sea | A rainforest with wet, hot days all year | *A flat grassland with hot summers, cold winters and little rain | A snowy mountain top
test: «Much of Ukraine was then a cold, dry grassland called the mammoth steppe.» What does dry tell you about the steppe? | It was covered in snow all year | It had many lakes and rivers | It was full of thick forests | *It had little rain
test: The prairie in North America and the pampas in South America are both grasslands. What other grassland is like them? | A desert of hot sand | *A steppe | A tropical rainforest | A coral reef
exam: Jayden reads «Nomads rode horses across the steppes.» What does steppes mean here? | Busy towns in the desert | *Huge, flat grasslands with few trees | Small hills with lots of trees | Deep, dark lakes
